Template: locales/locales_to_be_generated
Type: multiselect
Choices: ${locales}
Description: Locales to compile:
 A locale holds the conventions of a language and region: messages, dates,
 numbers, money, sorting and character classes. Each locale selected here is
 compiled by locale-gen into /usr/lib/locale/locale-archive and listed in
 /etc/locale.gen; a UTF-8 locale is the usual choice.

Template: locales/default_environment_locale
Type: select
Choices: None, ${locales}
Default: None
Description: Default locale of the system environment:
 The locale chosen here is written as LANG to /etc/locale.conf (update-locale),
 which login sessions read. None leaves LANG unset, so programs use the C
 locale unless the user sets one.
